# The Key to the Role

Every role has a **trust policy** (a JSON document) that specifies **who** is allowed to assume it. It looks similar to a regular policy but defines the `Principal` (the entity that can assume the role).

Example: Allow EC2 service to assume this role:
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": { "Service": "ec2.amazonaws.com" },
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
  }]
}
```
